  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">Project Prevent: Mitigating religious tensions and attacks</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">Proposed activities are designed to prevent and mitigate any future acts of religiously motivated violence in high-risk areas for religious violence, strengthen documentation of freedom of religion or belief (FoRB)  violations in tension-prone districts and engage in advocacy with key duty bearers at the local and national level to promote FoRB in Sri Lanka. Activities which will have an inter-religious focus, will involve establishing an early-warning and early response system in two identified districts which are high-risk areas for religious violence, setting up a network of rapporteurs who will document FoRB violations in 9 districts which are prone to religious tensions, monitoring social media for FoRB violations, analysing trends and patterns of FoRB violations in hotbed areas and carrying out advocacy with local and national-level state actors to escalate issues in the target districts and hold duty bearers responsible to protect and promote FoRB in Sri Lanka.</narrative>
  </description>
